In article <3770@orion.cf.uci.edu> easu021@orion.oac.uci.edu (Jason Goldberg) writes:
>1.  Other than their value to be polymorphed into other objects what do 
>    the following objects do?   Wand of nothing, Scroll of fire, Scroll
>    of blank paper, potion of fruit juice, Hawaiian Shirt.

Wand of nothing.  I have no idea what this might be good for.

Scroll of fire.  If you are fire resistant it will do fire damage to creatures
                 around you (I think).  But it may also destroy any potions or
                 scrolls you are carrying.  Not a praticularly useful scroll.

Scroll of blank paper.  Write the name of a scroll that you know on this
                        using a magic marker.  The results can be amazing. ;-)

Potion of fruit juice.  Gives you some nurishment.  About the same as eating
                        a fruit I think.

Hawaiian Shirt.  Good for enchanting if all of your other armor is enchanted
                 to the point where it might disintegrate if you attempt to
                 enchant it one more time.

I hope all of this helps.                                          Marc
